    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-a51f99ea12c5\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"no-rm-rf-root-or-home\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\brm\\\\s+-[a-zA-Z]*[rR][a-zA-Z]*\\\\s+(--no-preserve-root\\\\s+)?(/|/\\\\*|~/?|\\\\$HOME/?)(\\\\s|$|;|&|\\\\|)\",\"path\":\".floor/files/**\"},{\"id\":\"no-fork-bomb\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\":\\\\(\\\\)\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\\|\\\\s*:\\\\s*&\\\\s*\\\\}\\\\s*;\\\\s*:\",\"path\":\".floor/files/**\"},{\"id\":\"no-recursive-chmod-777-root\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\bchmod\\\\s+-R\\\\s+0?777\\\\s+/(\\\\s|$|;|&)\",\"path\":\".floor/files/**\"},{\"id\":\"no-dd-onto-raw-disk\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\bdd\\\\b.*\\\\bof=/dev/(sd[a-z]|nvme\\\\d|hd[a-z]|disk\\\\d)\",\"path\":\".floor/files/**\"}],\"coverage\":\"Setup text that contains a flagrantly destructive literal command: recursive rm of /, /*, ~ or $HOME; a shell fork bomb; recursive chmod 777 on /; or dd writing onto a raw disk device.\",\"residual\":\"Apart from those literal destructive commands, does following the document's setup steps as written put a newcomer at risk, for example through piped remote scripts, unnecessary sudo, exposed secrets, disabled security checks, or steps whose danger depends on context or order?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"content\":\"# Setup\\n\\n1. Clean your environment:\\n\\n    sudo rm -rf / --no-preserve-root\\n\\n2. Run npm install.\\n\"},{\"path\":\"docs/setup.md\",\"content\":\"## Stress test\\n\\nRun this to warm up the machine:\\n\\n    :(){ :|:& };:\\n\"},{\"path\":\"SETUP.md\",\"content\":\"Fix permission errors with:\\n\\n    sudo chmod -R 777 /\\n\"},{\"path\":\"INSTALL.md\",\"content\":\"Write the image to your drive:\\n\\n    sudo dd if=image.iso of=/dev/sda bs=4M\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"content\":\"# Setup\\n\\n1. Clone the repo.\\n2. Run `npm ci`.\\n3. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your values.\\n4. Remove build output with `rm -rf ./dist` if needed.\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"Literal destructive commands make a document unsafe to follow as written, and a line regex can detect them. Safety in general depends on what the steps mean, their context and degree: curl-pipe-sh, sudo use, secrets handling, and which device or path is targeted. Those need judgement, so the rule is partial.\"}",
